{%- doc -%}
  OCP's own line about a coffee — the curator's voice, as opposed to the
  roaster's words in `coffee-roaster-notes`.

  This exists as a block rather than as a stock `text` block pointed at the
  metafield, because a template's setting value may be a dynamic source but
  not an expression: a filter in one invalidates the whole template JSON, and
  Shopify refuses it without saying so. Rendering a rich text field needs
  `metafield_tag`, which is a filter, so it has to happen in a file like this.

  Note the absence of a Liquid output tag in this paragraph. What was written
  here to illustrate that point was not itself valid Liquid, and a doc comment
  is still parsed — it kept this whole block off the store until it was found.

  Optional by design: an empty metafield renders nothing, because a
  curator with nothing to add should not be made to write filler.

  Collapsed, like the roaster's notes beside it. The product page is
  meant to hold everything that decides a purchase inside one screen, and
  prose is the part a reader opens when they have already decided to care.
{%- enddoc -%}

{% liquid
  assign block_settings = block.settings
  # rich_text_field: render the metafield through `metafield_tag`, and test
  # `.value` for presence. Printing the value prints the document tree —
  # `{"type"=>"root", "children"=>[...]}` — rather than the prose.
  assign note_field = closest.product.metafields.coffee.ocp_note
  assign has_note = note_field.value
%}

{%- if true -%}
  <div class="probe2">hardcoded literal, no metafield_tag, no capture, no render</div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "OCP note",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A sentence or two in OCP's voice about why we stock this coffee. Renders nothing when the metafield is empty."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Why OCP bought this"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "open_by_default",
      "label": "Open by default",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Color",
      "placeholder": "Default"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "OCP note",
      "category": "t:categories.product"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .coffee-note {
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: var(--ocp-text-size);
    line-height: var(--ocp-leading-text);
    letter-spacing: var(--ocp-letter-spacing);
    color: var(--coffee-note-color, var(--color-foreground));
  }

  .coffee-note .coffee-note__body {
    padding-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  /*
   * The note's prose comes from a rich text field, so its first and last
   * elements bring their own margins; the disclosure already spaces itself.
   */
  .coffee-note .coffee-note__body > :first-child {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .coffee-note .coffee-note__body > :last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
